cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use B-ICE DeTRESer in your research, please cite the software using these metadata."
type: software
title: "B-ICE DeTRESer"
authors:
  - family-names: "Nicolella"
    given-names: "Zachary"
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Engineering Science, Osaka University"
  - family-names: "Morishita-Watanabe"
    given-names: "Nozomi"
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Engineering Science, Osaka University"
  - family-names: "Umakoshi"
    given-names: "Hiroshi"
    affiliation: "Graduate School of Engineering Science, Osaka University"
abstract: >-
  B-ICE DeTRESer is a desktop application for analysing time-resolved
  emission spectrum data exported by HORIBA DeltaFlex and EzTime systems.
  It supports TRES, decay-associated spectra, time-dependent fluorescence
  shifts, Laurdan generalized polarization and custom intensity ratios,
  time-resolved anisotropy, and optional microviscosity calculations.
keywords:
  - "time-resolved fluorescence"
  - "time-resolved emission spectra"
  - "TRES"
  - "decay-associated spectra"
  - "fluorescence anisotropy"
  - "Laurdan generalized polarization"
  - "membrane biophysics"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/znic1998/B-ICE-DeTRESer"
url: "https://github.com/znic1998/B-ICE-DeTRESer"
